en-US.text-clipper.usage:
**What it does**: clips web pages and fragments of text into your knowledge base in one move.

**How to use**:
1. Web clipping: top form on the sidebar "Plugins → Clipping" page → paste a URL → the body text is fetched and saved as a Markdown document, opening in the editor when done; clipping the same page twice is auto-deduplicated (opens the existing document);
2. Text clipping: anytime, tell Baize "Save this passage to the knowledge base" (or select text anywhere and trigger the selection shortcut → add "save to knowledge base"; defaults and effective keys for the selection/global shortcuts are in "Settings → Shortcuts");
3. Below the clipping page is the full clip history: click a row to open the document, click the source to revisit the original page, titles are the page titles — one-page recall.

**Notes**: clips are re-indexed on entry — immediately searchable, question-generatable, and graph-ready.

